Title:          fuzzel.tcz 
Description:    wlroots Applications launcher with fuzzy search as below
Version:        1.13.1
Author:         Daniel Eklöf
Original-site:  https://codeberg.org/dnkl/fuzzel
Copying-policy: Accompanied 
Size:           144K
Extension_by:   aus9 
Tags:           wlroots launcher fuzzy
Comments:       Install creates config at ~/.config/fuzzel/fuzzel.ini
                Add font TCEs if you do not like monospace
                Supports hicolor icon set in results
                This TCE mainly searches for *.desktop under
                /usr/local/share/applications so not a full
                launcher like dmenu or wofi This acts more like
                context menu to bring up Applications on libX/Xorg

                Launch from a terminal. You might see the 
                app you want to launch without searching
                -> Either mouse click to launch it OR
                use arrows to highlight line and press enter
                Otherwise start typing your search term,
                if nothing found suits you -> press Esc to quit
                If searching is giving only one result, no need
                to complete typing the full word just press enter

                Does not work on woodland

